worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_meaning_lexicon.js"
  ceiling 1460
  rationale "The seed meaning lexicon (roles, word forms, surfaces), program task and language detection, units, memory surfaces and the links-notation pattern matcher. Issue #658 cut this module out of one oversized worker file by line count; R1188-U5 named it after what it holds. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. The +8 lines over the previous 1388 ceiling are the only logic the framework-target widening needed anywhere in the mirror (issue #723): programLanguageFromPrompt consults framework rows before language rows, mirroring program_language_by_alias, so a request that names both -- `напиши мне код на PHP Laravel` -- resolves to the framework rather than to the language it is written in. Six of the eight lines are the comment saying why. This ordering moves to js/wasm-worker with the rest of the write-program surface. Issue #710 raised it from 1396 to 1398 for the two lines that route the browser mirror into the same recoveries. Ceiling moved 1393 to 1405 with the canonical operand order mirror for commutative tie-breaking. Ceiling moved 1405 to 1411 for the operation-vocabulary `exclude` forms ('smallest first' is an order, not a minimum), mirroring rust/src/seed/operation_vocabulary.rs. Ceiling 1426 (2026-10-07, R1017): text operations chain in the order the request names them (OperationVocabulary::position twin). Ceiling 1441 (2026-10-07, R1017): the operation vocabulary reads counting cues, unit nouns, character-class members and argument-before phrases, mirroring rust/src/seed/operation_vocabulary.rs. Ceiling 1459 (2026-10-08, issue #1165 R1165-4): codingOracleDocumentedSnippet lets the coding oracle answer from the documentation route before its cached snapshots, mirroring documented_oracle_program and oracle_snippet in Rust, so the Swift snapshot of formal_ai_worker_installation_and_software_followups.js is retired. Lowered to 1457 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): the incompatible-units sentence is the seeded unit_incompatibility response. Ceiling moved 1457 to 1460 (R1188-U5): the first comment lines say what the module holds."
